#~ "### Added\n"
#~ "- **Obligato mode (background music)** — Play a favourite station quietly "
#~ "in the background, on its own independent audio output and volume, no "
#~ "matter what plays (or doesn't play) as the main media.\n"
#~ "  - New shortcut: `Ctrl+Win+Shift+M` toggles Obligato mode on and off.\n"
#~ "  - On first press, a dialog lets you choose the background station (from "
#~ "your favourites), the output device (**Same as main output** by default, "
#~ "**System default**, or any specific device), and the background volume as "
#~ "a percentage of the main player's current volume (25%–150%). Your choices "
#~ "are remembered for next time.\n"
#~ "  - Runs on a fully separate playback engine from the main player, so "
#~ "switching stations, podcasts, or audio books — or stopping the main "
#~ "player entirely — never interrupts it.\n"
#~ "  - Background volume automatically stays proportional to the main "
#~ "player's volume as it changes (`Ctrl+Win+↑`/`↓`).\n"
#~ "  - Pausing the main player (`Ctrl+Win+P`) pauses the background station "
#~ "too, and resuming the main player resumes it; a full stop of the main "
#~ "player is not treated as a pause.\n"
#~ "  - Requires at least one favourite station; if none exist, FreeRadio "
#~ "prompts you to add one first.\n"
#~ "  - Start/stop announcements respect the **Mute notifications** setting.\n"
